Hudson Zestimate Action – Privacy Policy

Last updated: September 5, 2025

This Privacy Policy describes how the Hudson Zestimate Action (the “Action”) processes information when Hudson GPT retrieves a Zillow home value (Zestimate) through RapidAPI. This policy applies only to this Action and its integrations; your broader product and website may be covered by separate policies.

1) Who we are

Controller/Provider: Soulvere, Inc. (“Soulvere”, “we”, “us”, “our”)
Contact: aloha@soulvere.com

2) What this Action does

The Action sends a property address (or a zpid or property_url, if provided) to Zillow’s API via RapidAPI and returns a single numeric estimate (e.g., { "value": 287300 }).

Hudson GPT may use this number to display current home value and to calculate home value increase if you provide a prior baseline.

3) Information we process
3.1 Inputs we send to the API

Required (one of):

address (preferred and typically extracted from your Snapshot file), or

zpid, or

property_url

Headers:

X-Rapidapi-Key (your API key; configured in the Action’s secure settings)

(If your platform requires only one security scheme, we rely on the server domain to imply host.)

3.2 Information returned by the API

Zestimate value: { "value": <number> }

3.3 Metadata the systems may receive automatically

Technical logs (limited): timestamps, request/response sizes, error codes, and an action invocation ID.

Network metadata (by RapidAPI/Zillow): IP address, user-agent, and routing details typical for API requests.

We do not send names, emails, payment data, or other direct contact information to Zillow. However, a street address can be personal data if it identifies a natural person.

4) How we use the information

Provide the service: Fetch the current Zestimate for your report.

Compute analytics within your report: e.g., home_value_current_usd and, if a baseline exists, home_value_increase_usd.

Reliability & security: Troubleshoot errors, prevent abuse, and ensure availability.

We do not use Action data for cross-context behavioral advertising or to build unrelated profiles.

5) Legal bases (if GDPR/UK GDPR applies)

Performance of a contract (Art. 6(1)(b)): to return the requested estimate.

Legitimate interests (Art. 6(1)(f)): to keep the Action secure and reliable.

6) Sharing and third parties

We share only what’s necessary to operate the Action:

RapidAPI, LLC (API gateway) — receives the query and necessary headers.

Zillow Group Services — receives the address/zpid/property URL and returns the estimate.

These providers may process network metadata (e.g., IP) and are subject to their own privacy terms. We do not sell your data.

7) Retention

Action invocation data on our side: retained no longer than 30 days for security and debugging, then deleted or aggregated.

Zestimate values used in your report: stored in your report output as you direct.

No caching of API responses beyond generating the current report, unless you explicitly enable a “baseline capture” feature (in which case we store the prior value solely to compute future “increase” deltas).

You can request deletion of stored outputs via the contact below.

8) Security

Transport security: TLS for all requests.

Secrets management: API keys are stored in the Action’s encrypted configuration; never shown in reports or chat.

Data minimization: We send only what’s required (address or zpid).

Access controls & logging: Restricted access and minimal logs for operational needs.

No system is perfectly secure; we maintain administrative, technical, and physical safeguards appropriate to the risk.

9) International transfers

RapidAPI and Zillow may process data in the United States or other jurisdictions. Where applicable, we rely on lawful transfer mechanisms (e.g., SCCs) offered by our providers.

10) Your choices & rights

Don’t use the Action: You can generate reports without a Zillow estimate.

Review/delete outputs: Ask us to remove value outputs from stored reports.

Privacy rights: Depending on your location, you may have rights to access, correct, delete, or port your data, or to object/restrict certain processing. Contact us to exercise these rights.

11) Children’s data

This Action is not directed to children and is intended for adult homeowners and professionals.

12) “Do Not Sell or Share” (CCPA/CPRA)

We do not “sell” personal information or “share” it for cross-context behavioral advertising under California law.

13) Changes to this Policy

We may update this Privacy Policy as the Action evolves or laws change. Material changes will be communicated via release notes or admin channels.

